## Project-wide Font Size Correction

Resolved the issue where text elements appeared too small and illegible across all pages and tabs (Dashboard, Approvals, Reporting, User Management) of the application.

### 1. Scaling Standard Tailwind Typography Presets
Modified [tailwind.config.js](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/frontend/tailwind.config.js) under `theme.extend.fontSize` to scale up standard font-size utilities by ~1px to 2px:
- `text-xs`: Scaled from `12px` (`0.75rem`) to `13px` (`0.8125rem`)
- `text-sm`: Scaled from `14px` (`0.875rem`) to `15px` (`0.9375rem`)
- `text-base`: Scaled from `16px` (`1rem`) to `17px` (`1.0625rem`)
- `text-lg`: Scaled from `18px` (`1.125rem`) to `19px` (`1.1875rem`)
- `text-xl`: Scaled from `20px` (`1.25rem`) to `22px` (`1.375rem`)
- `text-2xl` / `text-3xl` / `text-4xl`: Scaled up proportionally to maintain hierarchy.

### 2. Base HTML Font Scaling & Micro-Font Class Overrides
Modified [index.css](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/frontend/src/index.css) to apply global CSS corrections:
- **Root Element Scaling**: Set `html { font-size: 109.375%; }` to scale up all `rem`-based font sizes and spacing metrics globally.
- **Tailwind Arbitrary Overrides**: Targeted absolute pixel-based utility classes (such as `text-[8px]`, `text-[9px]`, `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`, and `text-[12px]`) with `!important` declarations to map them to comfortable, readable font sizes (e.g. `text-[10px]` maps to `14.5px` and `text-[12px]` maps to `16px`).

